  <ferc:IdentificationOfSecuritiesIssuedOrAssumedAndSecuritiesRefundedOrRetiredTextBlock id="Tag1563" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;On March 6, 2025, Supply Corporation borrowed $25,000,000 from National Fuel Gas Company at an interest rate of 5.708%. The note matures on March 15, 2030. On the same date, Supply Corporation also borrowed $275,000,000 from National Fuel Gas Company at an interest rate of 6.119%. This note matures on March 15, 2035. The proceeds of these debt issuances were used to redeem $125,000,000 of 5.358% notes and $150,000,000 of 5.779% notes on March 6, 2025. These notes were originally scheduled to mature on July 15, 2025 and January 15, 2026, respectively. The 5.358% notes and 5.779% notes were redeemed for $125,271,363 and $151,405,826, respectively, plus accrued interest. The call premiums were recorded to Account 189, Unamortized Loss on Reacquired Debt, in March 2025. The remaining debt issuance proceeds were used for general operating purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:IdentificationOfSecuritiesIssuedOrAssumedAndSecuritiesRefundedOrRetiredTextBlock>
