&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation records revenue for natural gas transportation and storage services in New York and Pennsylvania at tariff-based rates regulated by the FERC. Customers secure their own gas supply and Supply Corporation provides transportation and/or storage services to move the customer-supplied gas to the intended location, including injections into or withdrawals from the storage field. This performance obligation is satisfied over time. The rate design for Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s customers generally includes a combination of volumetric or commodity charges as well as monthly &amp;#8220;fixed&amp;#8221; charges (including charges commonly referred to as capacity charges, demand charges, or reservation charges). These types of fixed charges represent compensation for standing ready over the period of the month to deliver quantities of gas, regardless of whether the customer takes delivery of any quantity of gas. The performance obligation under these circumstances is satisfied based on the passage of time and meter reads, if applicable, which correlates to the period for which the charges are eligible to be invoiced. The amount billable, as determined by the meter read and the &amp;#8220;fixed&amp;#8221; monthly charge, indicates the value to the customer, and is used for revenue recognition purposes by Supply Corporation as specified by the &amp;#8220;invoice practical expedient&amp;#8221; (the amount that Supply Corporation has the right to invoice) under the authoritative guidance for revenue recognition. Customers are billed after the end of each calendar month, with payment typically due by the 25th day of the month in which the invoice is received.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation expects to recognize the following revenue amounts in future periods related to &amp;#8220;fixed&amp;#8221; charges associated with remaining performance obligations for transportation and storage contracts: $316.2 million for calendar 2026; $260.3 million for calendar 2027; $117.3 million for calendar 2028; $104.7 million for calendar 2029; $95.9 million for calendar 2030; and $424.2 million thereafter.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;C - System Relations and Transactions:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation is an integrated member of the National Fuel Gas System (&amp;#8220;the System&amp;#8221;), which is engaged in all phases of the natural gas business. Principal relationships with National Fuel Gas Company (&amp;#8220;the Company&amp;#8221;) and the other subsidiaries within the System include providing storage and transportation services, financing operations through debt and stock issuance and receiving administrative and technical assistance.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The Company owns 100 percent of Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s $25 par value common stock. At December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were 1,013,802 shares of common stock authorized, issued and outstanding.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In the event Supply Corporation has short-term cash needs or excess cash, it can borrow from or lend to the System Money Pool (at nominal rates). The Company administers the Money Pool and coordinates the System&amp;#8217;s short-term borrowings. The Money Pool funds are derived from the following sources; (1) surplus funds of the Company and its subsidiaries; (2) proceeds from the Company&amp;#8217;s sale of commercial paper; (3) borrowings by the Company from banks and other financial institutions.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Operating revenues from affiliated companies, mainly related to the transportation and storage of gas for National Fuel Gas Distribution Corporation (Distribution Corporation), amounted to $150,333,920 and $148,927,693 for the fiscal years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024, respectively. The majority of the expenses from affiliated companies relate to interest on intercompany debt, borrowed labor from Distribution Corporation, inventory and allocations of information services, telecommunications network and general and administrative expenses from Distribution Corporation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;D - Income Taxes:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The components of federal and state income taxes included in the Statement of Income are as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 430.5pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;

&lt;tr style="height: 14.25pt; -aw-height-rule: exactly;"&gt;
