&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The Benefit Obligation was determined using an assumed discount rate as noted in the data above.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The discount rate increased from 4.98% in 2024 to 5.30% in 2025. This led to a $2,678,963 decrease in the Benefit Obligation. Claim costs, premiums, retiree contributions and retiree drug subsidy assumptions were updated which caused a $1,211,301 increase in the Benefit Obligation. The healthcare cost trend rates were updated which caused a $4,771,127 increase in the Benefit Obligation. In addition, there was a $1,592,607 increase in the Benefit Obligation due to the difference between expected demographic experience and actual results. The mortality improvement projection scale was updated. This led to a $60,764 decrease in the Benefit Obligation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In 2024, a discount rate decrease caused a $7,425,381 increase in the Benefit Obligation. There was a $434,610 increase in the Benefit Obligation due to updated claim costs, premiums, retiree contributions and retiree drug subsidy assumptions. The healthcare cost trend rates were updated which caused a $$6,289,470 increase in the Benefit Obligation. In addition, there was a $806,668 decrease in the Benefit Obligation due to the difference between expected demographic experience and actual results. The mortality improvement projection scale was updated. This led to a $12,122 decrease in the Benefit Obligation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
