&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The fair values disclosed in the above tables may not be indicative of net realizable value or reflective of future fair values. Furthermore, although Supply Corporation believes its valuation methods are appropriate and consistent with other market participants, the use of different methodologies or assumptions to determine the fair value of certain financial instruments could result in a different fair value measurement at the reporting date.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For the fiscal years ended September 30, 2025 and September 30, 2024, there were no transfers from Level 1 to Level 2. For the years ended September 30, 2025 and September 30, 2024, there were no assets measured at fair value and classified as Level 3.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s assumption regarding the expected long-term rate of return on plan assets is 7.10% and 6.10% for the Retirement Plan and other post-retirement benefits respectively, effective for fiscal 2026. The return assumption reflects the anticipated long-term rate of return on the plan&amp;#8217;s current and future assets. Supply Corporation utilizes projected capital market conditions and the plan&amp;#8217;s target asset class and investment manager allocations to set the assumption regarding the expected return on plan assets.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;G - Commitments and Contingencies:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Environmental Matters.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Supply Corporation is subject to various federal, state and local laws and regulations relating to the protection of the environment. Supply Corporation has established procedures for the on-going evaluation of its operations to identify potential environmental exposures and assure compliance with regulatory policies and procedures.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;It is Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s policy to accrue estimated environmental clean-up costs when such amounts can reasonably be estimated and it is probable that Supply Corporation will be required to incur such costs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation is involved in various environmental matters arising in the normal course of business, none of which are expected at this time to have a material effect on the financial condition of Supply Corporation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%;"&gt;&lt;font style="line-height: 112%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Other.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="line-height: 112%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; Supply Corporation is involved in other litigation and regulatory matters arising in the normal course of business. While the resolution of such litigation or regulatory matters could have a material effect on earnings and cash flows in the year of resolution, none of this litigation, and none of these regulatory matters are expected to have a material adverse effect on the financial condition of Supply Corporation at this time&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;H - Rate Case Proceedings:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s rate settlement was approved June 11, 2024 with rates effective February 1, 2024, and provides that Supply Corporation may make a rate filing for new rates to be effective at any time. As well, any party can make a filing under NGA Section 5. Supply Corporation has no rate case currently on file.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;I - Subsequent Events:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In accordance with the authoritative guidance for subsequent events, Supply Corporation has evaluated subsequent events through April 13, 2026, which represents the date the financial statements were available to be issued, in order to ensure that this Form No. 2 includes appropriate disclosure of events both recognized in the financial statements as of December 31, 2025, and events which occurred subsequent to December 31, 2025 but were not recognized in the financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperRoman'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 8.84pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;II.&lt;font style="width: 8.84pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;NOTES APPLICABLE TO BALANCE SHEET:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;J - Regulatory Matters:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Liabilities.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; Supply Corporation has incurred various costs and received various credits that have been reflected as regulatory assets and liabilities on its balance sheets. Accounting for such costs and credits as regulatory assets and liabilities is in accordance with the authoritative guidance which sets forth the application of generally accepted accounting principles for those companies whose rates are established by or are subject to approval by an independent third-party regulator. Under this guidance, regulated companies defer costs and credits on the balance sheet as regulatory assets and liabilities when it is probable that these costs and credits will be allowed in the rate setting process in a period different from the period in which they would have been reflected in income by an unregulated company. These deferred regulatory assets and liabilities are then flowed through the income statement in the period in which the same amounts are reflected in rates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation has recorded the following regulatory assets and liabilities at December 31:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
