&lt;td style="width: 66.75pt; border-top: 1pt solid #000000; border-bottom: 3pt double #000000; padding-right: 0.75pt; vertical-align: bottom;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.65pt; margin-bottom: 1.5pt; text-align: right; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 0.09pt; font-family: Arial; display: inline-block; -aw-tabstop-align: left; -aw-tabstop-pos: 5.65pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;569,683,748&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 3.19pt; font-family: Arial; display: inline-block; -aw-tabstop-align: left; -aw-tabstop-pos: 64.45pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 13.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The fair market value of Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s debt, as presented in the table above, was determined using a discounted cash flow model, which incorporates Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s credit risk and current market conditions in determining the yield, and subsequently, the fair market value of the debt. The fair value of Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s long-term debt was calculated using observable inputs (U.S. Treasuries or Secured Overnight Financing Rates (SOFR) for the risk-free component and company specific credit spread information - generally obtained from recent trade activity in the Company&amp;#8217;s debt). As such, Supply Corporation considers the debt to be Level 2.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On March 6, 2025, Supply Corporation borrowed $25,000,000 from the Company at an interest rate of 5.708%. The note matures on March 15, 2030. On the same date, Supply Corporation also borrowed $275,000,000 from the Company at an interest rate of 6.119%. This note matures on March 15, 2035. The proceeds of these debt issuances were used to redeem $125,000,000 of 5.358% notes and $150,000,000 of 5.779% notes on March 6, 2025. These notes were originally scheduled to mature on July 15, 2025 and January 15, 2026, respectively. The 5.358% notes and 5.779% notes were redeemed for $125,271,363 and $151,405,826, respectively, plus accrued interest. The call premiums were recorded to Account 189, Unamortized Loss on Reacquired Debt, in March 2025. The remaining debt issuance proceeds were used for general operating purposes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperRoman'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.51pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;III.&lt;font style="width: 5.51pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;NOTES APPLICABLE TO STATEMENT OF CASH FLOWS:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;L - Statement of Cash Flows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For purposes of the Statement of Cash Flows, Supply Corporation considers all highly liquid investments with a maturity of generally three months or less to be cash equivalents. Interest paid for the calendar years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 was $35,954,790 and $34,403,387, respectively. Net income taxes paid for the calendar years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $7,537,377 and $9,579,183, respectively. Federal and New York State income taxes are paid by the Company on a consolidated basis. Supply Corporation pays its share to the Company. Pennsylvania income taxes are paid directly by Supply Corporation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 40.5pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 112%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Supply Corporation has accounts payable and accrued liabilities recorded on its Balance Sheets that are related to capital expenditures. These amounts represent non-cash investing activities at the balance sheet date. Accordingly, they are excluded from the Statement of Cash Flows when they are recorded as liabilities and included in the Statement of Cash Flows when they are paid in the subsequent period. The following table summarizes Supply Corporation&amp;#8217;s non-cash capital expenditures recorded as Accounts Payable and Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities on the Balance Sheet:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
