    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value75" xlink:to="footnote75" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="75" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote76" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>On May 1, 2018, Supply Corporation entered into a capacity lease and service agreement with Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company. Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company leased to Supply Corporation 40,000 dth per day of transportation capacity along Tennessee's 200 line system between Supply Corporation's existing interconnections at East Aurora, NY and Mercer, PA. Tennessee will also provide interruptible transmission on a month-by-month basis to Supply Corporation as needed.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value76" xlink:to="footnote76" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="76" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote77" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Information by rate schedule is not available. In accordance with Supply Corporation's Tariff, Section 14.7, monthly imbalances for all agreements in effect for a single shipper are set off against each other to calculate the monthly shipper imbalance. Thus, imbalances are tracked by shipper (which may be operating under several rate schedules) and not by rate schedule. In addition, imbalances include those arising under Operation Balancing Agreements (OBAs) that have no related rate schedule.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value77" xlink:to="footnote77" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="77" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote78" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 21.7807%;" border="0">
          <xhtml:tbody>
            <xhtml:tr>
              <xhtml:td style="width: 20.6957%;">Non-Qualified Pension Plan</xhtml:td>
              <xhtml:td style="width: 2.77778%; text-align: right;">$75,494</xhtml:td>
            </xhtml:tr>
          </xhtml:tbody>
        </xhtml:table>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value78" xlink:to="footnote78" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="78" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote79" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 23.2935%; height: 60px;" border="0">
          <xhtml:tbody>
            <xhtml:tr style="height: 20px;">
              <xhtml:td style="width: 28.9458%; height: 20px;">Employer Match on 401(K)</xhtml:td>
              <xhtml:td style="width: 4.84974%; height: 20px; text-align: right;">$2,333,701</xhtml:td>
            </xhtml:tr>
            <xhtml:tr style="height: 20px;">
              <xhtml:td style="width: 28.9458%; height: 20px;">Defined Contribution Plan</xhtml:td>
              <xhtml:td style="width: 4.84974%; height: 20px; text-align: right;">1,616,531</xhtml:td>
            </xhtml:tr>
            <xhtml:tr style="height: 20px;">
              <xhtml:td style="width: 28.9458%; height: 20px;">
              </xhtml:td>
              <xhtml:td style="width: 4.84974%; height: 20px; text-align: right;border-top-width: 1pt ;border-top-style: solid ;border-top-color: #000000;border-bottom-width: 1pt ;border-bottom-style: solid ;border-bottom-color: #000000;">$3,950,232</xhtml:td>
            </xhtml:tr>
          </xhtml:tbody>
        </xhtml:table>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value79" xlink:to="footnote79" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="79" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote80" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is borrowed from associate companies at cost, including benefits, and is used to perform field work in the areas of production, storage, transmission and some administrative and general work. The cost of the borrowed labor is charged to a variety of accounts including: 107, 108, 163, 183, 184, 186, 426, 750, 753, 756, 757, 759, 762, 764, 767, 769, 814, 817, 818, 820, 824, 830, 831, 832, 833, 834, 835, 836, 850, 853, 856, 857, 859, 861, 862, 863, 865, 867, 920, 921, 925, 930, 932.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value80" xlink:to="footnote80" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="80" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote81" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Inventory costs relate to material that is transferred from an associate company's inventory into a Supply Corporation stockroom or issued directly to the work being performed. The inventory costs are charged to the following accounts: 107, 108, 146, 154, 163, 184, 186, 234, 495, 753, 756, 764, 767, 771, 807, 816, 817, 818, 820, 824, 831, 832, 833, 835, 836, 853, 856, 857, 859, 862, 863, 865, 867, 925, 930.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value81" xlink:to="footnote81" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="81" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote83" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is borrowed from associate companies at cost, including benefits, and is used to perform field work in the areas of production, storage, transmission and some administrative and general work. The cost of the borrowed labor is charged to a variety of accounts including: 107, 108, 163, 183, 184, 186, 232, 242, 426, 753, 756, 759, 764, 814, 817, 818, 820, 824, 831, 832, 833, 834, 835, 850, 853, 856, 857, 859, 860, 863, 865, 867, 920, 921, 925, 926, 932.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value83" xlink:to="footnote83" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="83" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote86" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Inventory costs relate to material that is transferred from an associate company's inventory into a Supply Corporation stockroom or issued directly to the work being performed. The inventory costs are charged to the following accounts: 107, 108, 146, 154, 163, 183, 184, 186, 232, 495, 753, 756, 759, 764, 769, 816, 817, 818, 820, 824, 831, 832, 833, 834, 835, 836, 850, 853, 856, 857, 859, 862, 863, 864, 865, 867, 903, 920, 921, 925, 930, 932.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value86" xlink:to="footnote86" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="86" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote89" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Inventory costs relate to material that is transferred from an associate company's inventory into a Supply Corporation stockroom or issued directly to the work being performed.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value89" xlink:to="footnote89" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="89" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote91" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts: 232, 236, 241, 242, 408, 920, 921, 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value91" xlink:to="footnote91" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="91" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote92" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts: 242, 408, 920, 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value92" xlink:to="footnote92" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="92" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote95" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts: 242, 408, 920, 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value95" xlink:to="footnote95" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="95" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote96" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts: 128, 232, 236, 241, 242, 408, 920, 921, 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value96" xlink:to="footnote96" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="96" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote99" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts 242, 408, 920 and 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value99" xlink:to="footnote99" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="99" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote100" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Labor is loaned to associated companies at cost, including benefits. The loaned labor is used to perform field related work as well as engineering and other administrative work. The costs credit accounts 232, 236, 241, 242, 408, 920, 921, 926.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value100" xlink:to="footnote100" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="100" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote105" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Information Services costs are the costs of operating and maintaining the overall corporate network and application systems. The costs are allocated based on device count and time spent by analysts on each system. The costs are charged to accounts: 107, 426, 832, 859, 920, 921.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value105" xlink:to="footnote105" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="105" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote112" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Transportation charges for use of vehicles and tools by Supply Corporation employees loaned to Midstream Companies. The charges credit account 184.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value112" xlink:to="footnote112" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="112" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote113" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges to associated companies. The charges relate to items such as labor and use of vehicles and tools by Supply Corporation employees loaned to associated companies, fringe benefits, miscellaneous allocations including transportation services and gas supply administration, plant system adjustments, health insurance, rentals, inventory, and miscellaneous other small charges. The charges credit accounts 108, 146, 163, 183, 184, 232, 234, 242, 419, 493, 921, 931.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value113" xlink:to="footnote113" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="113" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote114" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges from associated companies that are charged to many of the same accounts listed in these footnotes. The charges relate to items such as messenger services, the use of vehicles and tools by Supply Corporation employees loaned to associated companies, rentals, fringe benefits, information services allocations, and miscellaneous other small charges. The expenses were charged to: 107, 108, 146, 163, 183, 184, 232, 750, 753, 756, 757, 759, 762, 764, 767, 814, 817, 818, 820, 824, 830, 831, 832, 833, 834, 835, 836, 850, 853, 856, 857, 859, 861, 862, 863, 865, 867, 920, 921, 925, 926, 930, 931, 932.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value114" xlink:to="footnote114" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="114" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote115" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Common expense allocations are the administrative and general costs of certain "common" departments, whose costs are allocated to the subsidiaries that benefit from the work of those departments. The three factors used are operating and maintenance expense, net plant and MCF throughput. The costs are charged to the following accounts: 163, 921, 923, 926, 930, 931.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value115" xlink:to="footnote115" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="115" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote116" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Miscellaneous allocations are a combination of costs related to the following allocations and their respective allocation factors: messenger expense (number of mail routes), meter shop (number of meters/jobs shipped), telecom (employee count), Capital Tool Repair (number of tool repairs). The costs are charged to the following accounts: 184, 835, 865, 867, 921.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value116" xlink:to="footnote116" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="116" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote117" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges from associated companies that are charged to many of the same accounts as listed in these footnotes. The charges relate to items such as the use of vehicles and tools by the employees whose labor was loaned to Supply Corporation, fringe benefits, project costing adjustments, miscellaneous allocations (telecom, messenger expense, meter shop, capital tool repair), miscellaneous adjustments, and MCP &amp; CDD costs, and other items. Expenses were charged to: 107, 108, 143, 146, 163, 184, 186, 232, 242, 408, 426, 753, 756, 759, 764, 769, 814, 817, 818, 820, 824, 831, 832, 833, 834, 835, 850, 853, 856, 857, 859, 862, 863, 864, 865, 867, 920, 921, 923, 925, 926, 930, 932.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value117" xlink:to="footnote117" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="117" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote118" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges from associated companies that are charged to many of the same accounts as listed in these footnotes. The charges relate to items such loaned labor and fringe benefits as well as the use of vehicles and tools by the employees whose labor was loaned to Supply Corporation, miscellaneous allocations including transportation services, line of credit fees, miscellaneous adjustments, inventory, rent, and other items. Expenses were charged to accounts: 107, 146, 154, 163, 184, 186, 232, 242, 834, 864, 920, 921, 926, 931.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value118" xlink:to="footnote118" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="118" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote119" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges related to items such as labor and use of vehicles and tools by Supply Corporation employees loaned to associated companies, rentals, inventory, plant system adjustments and miscellaneous other small charges. The charges credit 107, 108, 154, 163, 183, 184, 232, 242, 432, 850, 863, 921, 923, 930, 931.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value119" xlink:to="footnote119" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="119" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote121" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The other category is a summation of charges related to items such as gas measurement and transportation services cost allocations, labor &amp; use of vehicles and tools by Supply Corporation employees loaned to associated companies, rentals, inventory and miscellaneous other small charges. The charges credit accounts: 154, 163, 184, 232, 242, 834, 859, 863, 864, 921, 931.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value121" xlink:to="footnote121" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="121" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote122" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>The date range for the Consecutive Three-Day Peak Deliveries was 2026-01-23 to 2026-01-25.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value122" xlink:to="footnote122" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="122" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote123" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Includes the Spring Creek compressor station. The Spring Creek compressor was retired as of May 22, 2018. Plant cost on the books represents meters and piping which will remain as gas is still free flowing. The Spring Creek compressor was a leased unit and has been removed.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value123" xlink:to="footnote123" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="123" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote124" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>This compressor station functions as both a transmission and storage compression facility. As these facilities do not have separate meters for fuel (i.e. natural gas) or electricity, the fuel and electricity for the station is assigned entirely to storage or transmission based on which function accounts for the majority of plant costs.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value124" xlink:to="footnote124" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="124" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote126" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>This compressor station functions as both a transmission and storage compression facility. As these facilities do not have separate meters for fuel (i.e. natural gas) or electricity, the fuel and electricity for the station is assigned entirely to storage or transmission based on which function accounts for the majority of plant costs.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value126" xlink:to="footnote126" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="126" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote128" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Two units at Ellisburg station are jointly owned with Dominion Transmission Corporation (35.65%). Supply Corporation's portion is 64.35%. Supply Corporation operates the station.</xhtml:p>
        <xhtml:p>Also, this compressor station functions as both a transmission and storage compression facility. As these facilities do not have separate meters for fuel (i.e. natural gas) or electricity, the fuel and electricity for the station is assigned entirely to storage or transmission based on which function accountsfor the majority of plant costs.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value128" xlink:to="footnote128" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="128" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote129" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>Lockport station is jointly owned with Tennessee Gas Pipeline (47.33%) and Dominion Transmission Corporation (8.32%). Supply Corporation's portion is 44.35%. Tennessee Gas Pipeline operates the station.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value129" xlink:to="footnote129" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="129" />
