    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value150" xlink:to="footnote150" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="150" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:label="footnote151" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <xhtml:div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <xhtml:p>This compressor station functioned as both a transmission and storage compression facility. As these facilities did not have separate meters for fuel (i.e. natural gas) or electricity, the fuel and electricity for the station was assigned entirely to storage or transmission based on which function accounted for the majority of plant costs.</xhtml:p>
        <xhtml:p>Boone Mountain compressor station previously had 2 compressor units that provided certified horsepower of 300. This station was abandoned in September 2025.</xhtml:p>
      </xhtml:div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:from="value151" xlink:to="footnote151" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" order="151" />
